  "final_message": "The recipe book app is complete and working end-to-end.\n\n## What was built\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask app with SQLite under `./data`:\n- Auth: `POST /api/auth/register` (201), `POST /api/auth/login` (returns `{token}`), token-based `Authorization: Bearer` with 401 on missing/invalid tokens.\n- Recipes: `POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /api/recipes` and `GET /api/recipes/{id}`; listing is paged (`category`, `q`, `page`, `page_size`) and omits ingredients/instructions; authors can only edit/delete their own (403 otherwise). Ingredients are stored as JSON to preserve order. Validation messages returned as `{error: ...}`.\n- Seeds 4 sample recipes across 4 categories on first start. Also added `GET /api/categories` for the frontend dropdown.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`) \u2014 React + TypeScript (Vite) with Tailwind CSS v4:\n- Register/sign-in forms, header with username + sign-out, add/edit forms with dynamic ingredient rows and API validation messages, delete confirmation modal, recipe cards with category/prep/author, category dropdown, title search, paging, and a detail page preserving instruction line breaks.\n\n**Verification**: full API flow tested (register/login/create/update/delete/403/401/validation/search/paging), `npm run build` succeeds, and the gunicorn server serves the API, frontend build, assets, and deep links correctly.\n\nNote: I added `@tailwindcss/vite`, `tailwindcss`, `react-router-dom`, and `typescript` to `package.json`/`package-lock.json` (typescript pinned to 5.9.3, since the resolved `^7.0.2` version requires a Node runtime not present in the Docker image).",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
